  "placed_for_low_flight": true,
  "camera_positions_note": "Camera positions and starting headings were chosen with last year's greedy idea re-implemented: each camera's view is a no-fly area and each round keeps the camera that most lengthens the attacker's shortest route (2 m grid), skipping any that leaves no route; stop below 5 m gain. Roof sites and 14 m poles on open ground (not on runways, taxiways or aprons) were allowed. The first 2 cameras were reserved for the runway crossing (one per runway: 10L/28R, 10C/28C), so cameras also see aircraft on those runways. The detour rule gives 0 m on open ground, so each is the allowed pole site nearest where the shortest unseen route crosses that runway, first looking at the crossing.",
